  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Stage two of a two-stage flow",
      "items": [
        "parl-worker calls tooth-recognition first, then feeds its result into this service",
        "The front itself is the standard twenty-line postgres-lro/lro setup",
        "It is still directly callable; nothing about the front assumes an orchestrator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Readiness instead of retries",
      "items": [
        "There is no computeRetries loop; the worker calls Compute exactly once per item",
        "main.go passes an inline ComputeReadinessCheck closure into ProcessWorkItemTaskConfig",
        "The pod stays unready until the sidecar answers, so cold start never reaches a claim"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two drifts worth fixing",
      "items": [
        "The Go container declares no resources block at all, so it is unbounded on the node",
        "The sidecar limits CPU to 5 but sets no memory limit, while requesting 25Gi",
        "Its image is pinned to cbctai-periapical-radiolucency-detection-compute:20250717"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Operations",
      "items": [
        "Datadog monitors live in infrastructure/platform/common/mle/constants.tf",
        "LRO duration threshold is 180s under opdoc DIA-023; the worker is DIA-024",
        "The parent parl service is DIA-021 at 300s and parl-worker is DIA-022"
      ]
    }
  ]
